  "reasoning": "Octopuses possess three hearts: two branchial hearts that pump deoxygenated blood through the gills to collect oxygen, and one systemic heart that pumps the oxygenated blood throughout the rest of the body. Furthermore, their blood is blue because it uses the copper-based protein hemocyanin rather than the iron-based hemoglobin found in vertebrates to transport oxygen, which appears blue when oxygenated and is adapted for cold, low-oxygen marine environments.",
